IMPORT prelude

-- Electronic Transactions Act 2010 (Singapore) -- electronic transferable records (Part 2A), secure electronic
-- records and signatures (Part 3), and the digital-signature rules in the Third Schedule.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electronic Transactions Act 2010 -- transferable records and secure signatures`

§§ `16D -- consent, and all-or-nothing derogation`

-- s 16D(1): "Nothing in this Part requires a person to use an electronic transferable record without the person's
-- consent." (2): consent "may be inferred from the person's conduct". (3): "(a) the parties who do not consent ...
-- may derogate from ALL the provisions of this Part; but (b) the parties may NOT derogate from ONLY SOME but not all".
--
-- Contrast s 5(3), which lets parties pick and choose among ss 6 and 11 to 16. Part 2A is all or nothing.
DECLARE Derogation IS ONE OF
    `none of Part 2A`
    `some of Part 2A`
    `all of Part 2A`

GIVEN `the derogation` IS A Derogation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the derogation is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the derogation`
    WHEN `some of Part 2A` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `16H, 16I, 16O -- what makes an electronic transferable record`

-- s 16H(1): a rule of law requiring a transferable document (a bill of exchange, a promissory note, a bill of lading)
-- is met by an electronic record if "(a) the electronic record contains the information that would be required ...; and
-- (b) a reliable method is used -- (i) to identify that electronic record as the AUTHORITATIVE electronic record ...;
-- (ii) to render that electronic record capable of being subject to CONTROL from its creation until it ceases to have
-- any effect or validity; and (iii) to retain the INTEGRITY of that electronic record."
-- s 16I: possession is met by a reliable method "(a) to establish EXCLUSIVE CONTROL ... by a person; and (b) to
-- identify that person as the person in control". Transfer of possession is transfer of control.
-- s 16O(1): "reliable" means "(a) as reliable as appropriate ... in the light of all the relevant circumstances" or
-- "(b) proven in fact to have fulfilled the function".
-- s 16O(2), (3): a method is PRESUMED reliable, unless evidence to the contrary is adduced, if the record was issued,
-- transferred, controlled, presented AND stored on an accredited system of a registered provider DURING the period of
-- registration.
DECLARE TransferableRecord HAS
    `contains the information the paper document would need` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identifies the authoritative record by a reliable method` IS A BOOLEAN
    `subject to control from creation to end by a reliable method` IS A BOOLEAN
    `integrity retained by a reliable method` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exclusive control established by a reliable method` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person in control identified by a reliable method` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the record` IS A TransferableRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record is an electronic transferable record` IF
        `the record`'s `contains the information the paper document would need`
    AND `the record`'s `identifies the authoritative record by a reliable method`
    AND `the record`'s `subject to control from creation to end by a reliable method`
    AND `the record`'s `integrity retained by a reliable method`

GIVEN `the record` IS A TransferableRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person has possession of the record` IF
        `the record is an electronic transferable record` `the record`
    AND `the record`'s `exclusive control established by a reliable method`
    AND `the record`'s `the person in control identified by a reliable method`

DECLARE SystemUse HAS
    `on an accredited system of a registered, licensed, accredited or recognised provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `issued there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `transferred there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `controlled there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `presented there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stored there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all during the provider's registration` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A SystemUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reliability is presumed under section 16O(2)` IF
        `the use`'s `on an accredited system of a registered, licensed, accredited or recognised provider`
    AND `the use`'s `issued there`
    AND `the use`'s `transferred there`
    AND `the use`'s `controlled there`
    AND `the use`'s `presented there`
    AND `the use`'s `stored there`
    AND `the use`'s `all during the provider's registration`

§§ `16M, 16N -- change of medium`

-- s 16M: paper to electronic. The change takes effect only if "(a) ALL the information ... [is] accurately reproduced"
-- and "(b) a STATEMENT indicating a change of medium [is] inserted". Then the paper "(a) ceases to have any effect or
-- validity; and (b) must be made inoperative." s 16M(4): rights and obligations are unaffected.
-- s 16N: electronic to paper, the same; but s 16N(3): the information to be reproduced "does not include any additional
-- information that may be contained in an electronic transferable record mentioned in section 16C" (metadata, dynamic
-- data such as a vessel's position).
DECLARE ChangeOfMedium HAS
    `paper to electronic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reliable method is used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the core information is accurately reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the section 16C additional information is reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a statement of the change of medium is inserted` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the change` IS A ChangeOfMedium
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change of medium takes effect` IF
        `the change`'s `a reliable method is used`
    AND `the change`'s `the core information is accurately reproduced`
    AND `the change`'s `a statement of the change of medium is inserted`

-- Either direction, the information to reproduce is the information in the document being replaced. Paper has no
-- section 16C additional information; going to paper, s 16N(3) excuses it. So dropping metadata or dynamic data
-- never defeats a change of medium.

GIVEN `the change` IS A ChangeOfMedium
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the replaced document ceases to have effect` IF
    `the change of medium takes effect` `the change`

§§ `17, 18 -- secure electronic records and signatures`

-- s 17(1): where "a specified security procedure, or a commercially reasonable security procedure AGREED TO BY THE
-- PARTIES involved, has been properly applied to an electronic record to verify that [it] has not been altered since
-- a specific point in time, such record is treated as a secure electronic record from such specific point in time to
-- the time of verification."
-- s 18(1): a signature is a secure electronic signature if, through such a procedure, it can be verified that it was,
-- at the time it was made, "(a) unique to the person using it; (b) capable of identifying such person; (c) created in a
-- manner or using a means under the SOLE CONTROL of the person using it; and (d) linked to the electronic record ... such
-- that if the record was changed the electronic signature would be invalidated".
-- Second Schedule: the only specified security procedure is "Digital signatures, as defined in the Third Schedule".
DECLARE Procedure IS ONE OF
    `a specified security procedure`
    `a commercially reasonable procedure agreed by the parties`
    `a commercially reasonable procedure not agreed`
    `an unreasonable procedure agreed by the parties`
    `no procedure`

GIVEN `the procedure` IS A Procedure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the procedure qualifies under sections 17 and 18` IF
    CONSIDER `the procedure`
    WHEN `a specified security procedure` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a commercially reasonable procedure agreed by the parties` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE SignatureFacts HAS
    `the procedure` IS A Procedure
    `properly applied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unique to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `capable of identifying the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under the sole control of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `invalidated if the record changes` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the signature` IS A SignatureFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is a secure electronic signature` IF
        `the procedure qualifies under sections 17 and 18` (`the signature`'s `the procedure`)
    AND `the signature`'s `properly applied`
    AND `the signature`'s `unique to the person`
    AND `the signature`'s `capable of identifying the person`
    AND `the signature`'s `under the sole control of the person`
    AND `the signature`'s `invalidated if the record changes`

GIVEN `the procedure` IS A Procedure, `properly applied to verify no alteration since a point in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record is a secure electronic record` IF
        `the procedure qualifies under sections 17 and 18` `the procedure`
    AND `properly applied to verify no alteration since a point in time`

§§ `19 -- presumptions`

-- s 19(1): a secure electronic record is presumed unaltered since the point in time its status relates to.
-- s 19(2): a secure electronic signature is presumed to be the signature of the person it correlates to, and affixed
-- with the intention of signing or approving. Both rebuttable ("unless evidence to the contrary is adduced").
-- s 19(3): "In the absence of a secure electronic record or a secure electronic signature, nothing in this Part creates
-- any presumption relating to the authenticity and integrity".
GIVEN `the signature` IS A SignatureFacts, `evidence to the contrary is adduced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is presumed to be the person's, affixed with intent to sign` IF
        `the signature is a secure electronic signature` `the signature`
    AND NOT `evidence to the contrary is adduced`

§§ `Third Schedule -- digital signatures`

-- para 3: a digital signature is a secure electronic signature for the signed portion if "(a) [it] was created during
-- the operational period of a VALID certificate and is verified by reference to the public key listed in such
-- certificate; and (b) the certificate is considered trustworthy ... because -- (i) ... issued by an ACCREDITED
-- certification authority ...; (ii) ... by a RECOGNISED certification authority; (iii) ... by a PUBLIC AGENCY approved by
-- the Minister ...; or (iv) the parties have EXPRESSLY AGREED between themselves (sender and recipient) to use digital
-- signatures as a security procedure, and the digital signature was properly verified by reference to the sender's
-- public key."
-- para 1(1): "valid certificate" means one the CA has issued "and which the subscriber listed in it has accepted";
-- "operational period" ends on expiry, revocation or suspension.
DECLARE Issuer IS ONE OF
    `an accredited certification authority`
    `a recognised certification authority`
    `a public agency approved by the Minister`
    `an unaccredited commercial authority`
    `the subscriber itself`

DECLARE DigitalSignature HAS
    `the issuer` IS AN Issuer
    `the subscriber accepted the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `created within the certificate's operational period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `verified by the public key in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sender and recipient expressly agreed to use digital signatures` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the signature` IS A DigitalSignature
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is trustworthy under paragraph 3(b)` IF
        (CONSIDER `the signature`'s `the issuer`
            WHEN `an accredited certification authority` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a recognised certification authority` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a public agency approved by the Minister` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
    OR  (    `the signature`'s `sender and recipient expressly agreed to use digital signatures`
         AND `the signature`'s `verified by the public key in the certificate`)

GIVEN `the signature` IS A DigitalSignature
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the digital signature is a secure electronic signature` IF
        `the signature`'s `the subscriber accepted the certificate`
    AND `the signature`'s `created within the certificate's operational period`
    AND `the signature`'s `verified by the public key in the certificate`
    AND `the certificate is trustworthy under paragraph 3(b)` `the signature`

-- para 23(1): a subscriber is DEEMED to have accepted a certificate by publishing it (to one or more persons or in a
-- repository) or "otherwise demonstrat[ing] approval ... while knowing or having notice of its contents".
GIVEN `published or authorised publication of it` IS A BOOLEAN, `otherwise demonstrated approval knowing its contents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subscriber is deemed to have accepted the certificate` IF
    `published or authorised publication of it` OR `otherwise demonstrated approval knowing its contents`

§§ `Third Schedule para 11 -- the certification authority's liability cap`

-- para 11: "Unless [it] waives the application of this paragraph", an accredited, public or recognised CA "shall not be
-- liable -- (a) for any loss caused by reliance on a false or forged digital signature of a subscriber, if ... [it]
-- complied with the requirements of this Act; or (b) in excess of the amount specified in the certificate as its
-- recommended reliance limit" for a misrepresentation in the certificate or failure to comply with paras 14 and 15.
-- para 10: such a CA "must ... specify a recommended reliance limit in the certificate".
--
-- Liability under (b) is capped at the reliance limit whether or not the CA was at fault: the cap applies precisely
-- where the CA failed to follow the issuance rules.
DECLARE CALoss HAS
    `the CA is accredited, public or recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CA waived paragraph 11` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss was caused by a forged signature of a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CA complied with the Act as to that signature` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss was caused by a misrepresentation in the certificate or a breach of paragraphs 14 and 15` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss` IS A NUMBER
    `the recommended reliance limit` IS A NUMBER
    `the CA's liability apart from paragraph 11` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the claim` IS A CALoss
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 11 protects the CA` IF
        `the claim`'s `the CA is accredited, public or recognised`
    AND NOT `the claim`'s `the CA waived paragraph 11`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A CALoss
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the CA is wholly excused for the forged signature` IF
        `paragraph 11 protects the CA` `the claim`
    AND `the claim`'s `the loss was caused by a forged signature of a subscriber`
    AND `the claim`'s `the CA complied with the Act as to that signature`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A CALoss
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reliance limit caps the CA's liability` IF
        `paragraph 11 protects the CA` `the claim`
    AND `the claim`'s `the loss was caused by a misrepresentation in the certificate or a breach of paragraphs 14 and 15`

GIVEN `p` IS A NUMBER, `q` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `p` LESS THAN `q` THEN `p` ELSE `q`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A CALoss
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the CA can be liable for` MEANS
    IF `the CA is wholly excused for the forged signature` `the claim`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the reliance limit caps the CA's liability` `the claim`
         THEN `the smaller of` (`the claim`'s `the CA's liability apart from paragraph 11`) (`the claim`'s `the recommended reliance limit`)
         ELSE `the claim`'s `the CA's liability apart from paragraph 11`

§§ `Third Schedule paras 16 to 18, 25 -- suspension and revocation`

-- para 16: unless agreed otherwise, the CA "must suspend the certificate as soon as possible after receiving a request
-- by a person whom the certification authority reasonably believes to be -- (a) the subscriber ...; (b) a person duly
-- authorised to act for that subscriber; or (c) a person acting on behalf of that subscriber, WHO IS UNAVAILABLE."
--
-- Limb (c) needs no authority: anyone the CA reasonably believes to be acting for an unavailable subscriber can have a
-- certificate suspended.
DECLARE Requester IS ONE OF
    `the subscriber`
    `a person duly authorised by the subscriber`
    `a person acting for a subscriber who is unavailable`
    `a person acting for a subscriber who is available`
    `a stranger`

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `the CA reasonably believes the requester is who they claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `the CA and subscriber agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the CA must suspend the certificate` IF
        `the CA reasonably believes the requester is who they claim`
    AND NOT `the CA and subscriber agreed otherwise`
    AND CONSIDER `the requester`
        WHEN `the subscriber` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person duly authorised by the subscriber` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person acting for a subscriber who is unavailable` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- para 18(1): the CA must revoke WITHOUT the subscriber's consent if it confirms (a) a material fact represented is
-- false, (b) an issuance requirement was not satisfied, (c) its private key or trustworthy system was compromised, (d) an
-- individual subscriber is dead, or (e) the subscriber has ceased to exist.
-- para 18(2): "other than under sub-paragraph (1)(d) or (e), the certification authority must immediately notify the
-- subscriber".
DECLARE RevocationGround IS ONE OF
    `a material fact in the certificate is false`
    `an issuance requirement was not satisfied`
    `the CA's private key or system was compromised`
    `the individual subscriber is dead`
    `the subscriber has ceased to exist`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A RevocationGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the CA must notify the subscriber of the revocation` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the individual subscriber is dead` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the subscriber has ceased to exist` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- para 5: unless otherwise provided, a person relying on a digitally signed record "assumes the risk that the digital
-- signature is invalid" if reliance "is not reasonable under the circumstances".
GIVEN `reliance was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `law or contract provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relying party bears the risk of an invalid signature` IF
        NOT `reliance was reasonable`
    AND NOT `law or contract provides otherwise`
